# Project Purpose

- Speed up prototype design and authoring of UI definitions.
- Treat an abstracted **IR (Intermediate Representation)** as the domain core and **SSOT (Single Source Of Truth)**.
- Use the IR to convert to/from UI-framework (and other vendor) definition files.
- Maximize portability; minimize dependence on specific tech stacks or platform vendors.

## Core implication

All durable meaning about a UI definition lives in **IRDefinition**. External formats are adapters around it, not the source of truth.

## Documentation implication

Living docs under `docs/` keep the same split: **Core** documents IR and cross-cutting pipelines; **adapter target** details (vendor vocabulary, merge/serialize dialects, type maps) live in target-specific docs. See `.cursor/rules/12-docs-maintenance.mdc` (Core vs adapter target docs).

## Terminology in `.mdc` rules

When writing or editing project rules (`.mdc`), spell out project acronyms on use:

- Write **`SSOT (Single Source Of Truth)`** — do not use bare `SSOT` alone.
- Prefer the same pattern for other project acronyms when first introduced in a rule file.
